{title: 570 - Not I, But Christ}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #570 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 570}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Not I, but [Bb7]Christ, be honored, [Eb]loved, [Bb7]ex[Eb]alted;
[Ab]Not I, [Eb]but Christ, be seen, be [Bb7]known, [Eb]be [Bb]heard;
[Eb]Not I, [Bb7]but Christ, in [Cm7]every [Bb7]look and [Ab]ac[Eb]tion,
[Eb]Not I, [Bb7]but [Eb]Christ, [Ab]in [Bb7]every thought and [Eb]word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Not [Bb7]I, but [Eb]Christ, to [Bb7]gently soothe [Eb]in sorrow,
[Ab]Not [Eb]I, but [Bb7]Christ, to [Eb]wipe the [Bb]falling tear;
[Eb]Not [Bb7]I, but [Cm7]Christ, [Bb7]to lift [Ab]the [Eb]weary burden,
[Eb]Not [Bb7]I, but [Eb]Christ, [Ab]to hush [Bb7]away [Eb]all fear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Christ, [Bb7]only Christ! [Eb]No [Bb7]idle words [Eb]e'er falling,
[Ab]Christ, [Eb]only [Bb7]Christ; no [Eb]needless [Bb]bustling sound;
[Eb]Christ, [Bb7]only [Cm7]Christ, [Bb7]no [Ab]self [Eb]important bearing;
[Eb]Christ, [Bb7]only Christ, [Eb]no [Ab]trace of [Bb7]"I" [Eb]be found.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]Not [Bb7]I, but [Eb]Christ, [Bb7]my every [Eb]need supplying,
[Ab]Not I, [Eb]but Christ, [Bb7]my strength [Eb]and health [Bb]to be;
[Eb]Christ, [Bb7]only [Cm7]Christ, for [Bb7]body, [Ab]soul, [Eb]and spirit,
[Eb]Christ, [Bb7]only [Eb]Christ, [Ab]here [Bb7]and [Eb]eternally.
{end_of_verse}
